// The code an HTML file holds: a `<script>`'s text as JavaScript or JSON, by its `type`, and a `<style>`'s text as
// CSS. Each is a whole program at its element's `raw_text`, so its nodes have the file's lines and columns.
//
//   <script>let a = f(1);</script>               JavaScript: no type
//   <script type="module">…</script>             JavaScript: a JavaScript type, or "module"
//   <script type="application/ld+json">…</script> JSON: a JSON type, or "importmap"
//   <script type="text/template">…</script>      no program: a type the registry parses no grammar for
//   <style>p { color: red; }</style>             CSS
//
// The HTML language declares these programs (decision 0431 §4: `languages/html.json`'s `embeds`, built by
// `embed::raw_text` from the file's tape at its load), so this library derives nothing: a rule reaches a program
// through `parsed(r, "javascript", p)` at the `raw_text` r, as it did when the rules here made them (decision 0238).
